WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.167
-Last time we saw each other,

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.334
if you can believe this...

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:06.067
-The world was ending.
-...March 12, 2020.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:07.834
-Yes, sir.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.968
-What do you remember?
-Everything.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.634
-I know, I kind of remember it,
too, I think.

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:13.601
-It was bizarre.
I remember getting here

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.667
for sound check
because we were performing.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:16.834
-So you were already here.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:20.067
-I was here, in New York,
and I remember that

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.868
between sound check
and when we actually filmed,

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.133
there was apparently
supposed to be an audience

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.467
and then no audience.
-Yes.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.767
-Yeah, and it was like
Rockefeller Center

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.534
was shutting down,
New York City was shutting down.

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.000
It was terrifying.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.801
-Yeah, we were the only people
in the building.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.067
I think it was us
and the "Today" show, I think.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.100
-I think so.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.801
-Like, Savannah and Hoda
just stayed over.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.334
They're like, "All right, yeah,
don't leave the building."

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:40.400
-Hunker down.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.534
-We didn't know
what was going down.

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:42.901
And we were supposed
to have an audience.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:45.901
All our jokes are written
for an audience, and just no.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.734
-And then, I performed
for an empty theater.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:49.534
It was truly bizarre.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.267
No, no, it's okay.
The world --

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.801
[ Laughter ]
There was bigger fish to fry,

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:56.534
but it was -- I'll never, ever
forget that experience.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.734
-Yeah, I'm always here for you,
just so you know.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.334
I was always here.
I watched you.

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.367
I was like,
"Hey, if you need me."

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.534
-I felt the love.
-Okay, good.

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:03.601
-Yeah.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:04.901
-But a lot has happened
since then.

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.367
I'm so happy to see you.
You look great.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.968
-Thank you.
-But since we last talked,

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.667
since you were here,
you had a little baby boy.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.200
-I did.
-Congratulations.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah, thank you.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.868
-1 year old?
-Yeah, he's 14 months.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:20.367
-Mandy's got a cute name,
and he's such a cute baby.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.901
I want to show a picture,
if you don't mind.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.033
-Yeah, of course.
That's Gus.

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.968
-This is Gus.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.634
Look at this baby boy!

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.801
Come on, that's cute.

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:30.000
-My little man.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.167
-Oh, he's so cute.
Congratulations.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.400
-Thank you.
-He's pretty little.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.534
Is he into anything right now,
or is he too little?

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.667
-He's walking and talking
and doing all the things, yeah.

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.033
-Oh, he is?
-Yes.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.534
-Yeah.
-"Mama" was his first word.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.067
-I was gonna ask,
"Was it 'mama'?"

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.934
It was.
-I won!

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
I won.

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:49.234
-The first time
that you were a guest on here,

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.467
I think, was six years ago.

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.334
It was just when "This Is Us"
was premiering.

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.734
-Yes.
-And now, the series finale

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.434
is two weeks away.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.334
It's kind of interesting, right?
-Bizarre, yeah.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:01.334
-It's bizarre,
but I'm happy to see --

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.100
That's what I kind of love
about doing the show

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.434
is that you get to see

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:06.234
everyone's career
and start and things.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:09.167
And you get big.
-Yeah, an entire chapter.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.167
-Entire -- I mean --
-A really seminal chapter

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.667
for me, but, yeah.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.167
-Next two episodes
are coming up.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.400
Obviously no spoilers,
but on the emotional scale,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.901
1 being not that emotional
10 being "This Is Us"...

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:21.968
-Yeah.

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.267
Jack dying.
-Yes.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.133
Milo's character dying.
-Yes.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.200
-I would say --
I will tell you that

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:31.234
the penultimate episode,
which airs in like a week,

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:34.067
I threw up after I read it.
-Ooh!

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.801
-And maybe that's just because

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:37.801
it's really close
to the bone for me.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:40.000
Like, this has been my life
for the last six years.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.033
And it's like I simultaneously
have to say goodbye

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.901
to the character,
to my family and friends on set,

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.734
and this character's also,
coincidentally,

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.701
saying goodbye, as well.

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:51.834
So there was a lot
wrapped up in it.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.400
But I still think that, like,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.467
you might need a day off
from work.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:57.267
-Really?
It's one of those gems?

00:02:57.267 --> 00:03:00.133
-But the finale
is a bit more of a hug.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.834
I think there's a little bit
more levity.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.701
Yeah, the second-to-last is --
it destroyed me.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.434
I have a feeling it might
destroy people, too.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.801
-Well, I know
that your show is --

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:11.801
it's so well-written
and so --

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.901
It's very, like, tricky
and beautifully done.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.701
-Yes.
-And there's parts of

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:18.300
the next two episodes
that were filmed

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.901
three years ago.
-Yes.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.467
And I didn't even remember.
So, the finale,

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:24.267
the very last episode
of the show,

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:26.801
just because of the way
we tell the story

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.501
and jump around in time
and obviously, like,

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.868
children keep growing
and getting older,

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:34.934
we wanted to capture a very
particular time in their lives.

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:38.000
And so, some of the finale
was filmed three years ago.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.133
And I didn't even remember.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.300
Dan Fogleman, our creator,
was showing us a couple

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.200
of those scenes, and I'm like,
"Wow, I don't even --"

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.033
We weren't even halfway--
-He knew it in his head

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.801
and had written it, yes.
-Had written it.

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.300
-And just saved it for
the last episode, yeah.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.601
-He's brilliant.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.400
Did you take anything
from the set when you left?

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.434
-I did.
-You can tell people now, right?

00:03:57.434 --> 00:04:00.567
-Milo and I went
and did one last lap

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.634
through the Pearson house
and took some of

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:05.767
the family photos off the wall
and just put the frames back up.

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:07.100
[ Laughter ]
I mean, they were gonna

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.667
throw these pictures away,
anyway.

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.033
But they meant something to us.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:13.968
I took the Steelers jersey
from the Super Bowl episode.

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:16.501
I took my wedding ring.
My character's wedding ring.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.501
Yeah, I'm --
like, the sentimental things

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.801
were something
I wanted to take with me.

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.701
-Those photos must be
interesting because you probably

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:22.934
took them before you even
really knew each other.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.367
-Knew each other, yeah.

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.367
There's, like, all these, like,
fake photos of me laughing

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:28.834
with Milo, and we just
had met each other.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.400
We're supposed to be
husband and wife.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.400
-I think -- I don't know
if you knew this,

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.567
but when you first
get into this show,

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:38.200
did you realize you were gonna
play yourself -- your character

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.434
as a teenager
and as an 80-year-old woman?

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:44.667
-No. So, when your originally --
you audition and you're cast

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.734
for, like, the pilot,
the first episode

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:49.033
of a televisions show before it
ever gets picked up

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.567
and sees the light of day,
the character

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.000
was just written in this --

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.801
You know, I'm in the hospital,
giving birth to triplets,

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.634
and that's kind of
all you see of me.

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:00.834
I had no idea the scale
and the breadth

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:02.868
of what this matriarch
was gonna be.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.400
So it wasn't until about
two weeks

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.300
before we started shooting
the second episode

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:09.868
that I got an e-mail saying,
"So, we want to see

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:13.801
if it works for you to play
this character present-day."

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:17.234
And remember my mind just sort
of exploding like, "Wait.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:20.100
So, I'm gonna be working with
Sterling K. Brown

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.968
and Justin Har--
And I'm playing their mother.

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:24.033
I'm eight years younger
than them in real life.

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:27.501
It was a terrifying prospect.
-But what an acting --

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.701
what a gift.
-The greatest gift of all.

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:31.367
-You got to stretch.
And you nailed it, bud.

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.934
Everything, I'm like,
"Oh, that was so well done,"

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:35.934
and you really nailed it.
-Thank you.

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Really awesome.

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:39.901
Awesome job.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:43.300
Here's Mandy Moore in the final
season of "This Is Us."

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.901
Take a look.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:49.234
-Miguel?

00:05:49.234 --> 00:05:51.968
[ Groans ]

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:53.434
Miguel?

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:54.267
Miguel?!

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:57.000
-Ms. Pearson, it's okay.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.434
-Who are you?
-You're okay.

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:00.200
-Where's Miguel?
-It's okay.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.434
-I want Miguel.
I need Miguel!

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:03.801
-Hey, Mom, you're okay.

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:05.667
-Why won't this woman tell me
where Miguel is?

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.634
Where is Miguel?

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:08.934
-He's not here right now.

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:11.133
-Where is he?

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.634
-I got it.
Thank you.

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:17.267
Oh, Mom.
Gonna get you back in bed, Mom.

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:18.934
-Thank you.
-Where is Miguel?

00:06:18.934 --> 00:06:23.400
♪♪

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.934
-Yeah, Mandy Moore, everybody.

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.634
We're talking more with Mandy
after the break.

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:30.634
Stick around. Come on back.
We're talking records.

